ding «Guerrera», «Vaselina» and «Basta Ya»; a second, «La Palabra Amigo» (1983), was led by its title track; and a third, gold-pressed «Expresa e Interpreta Sus Sentimientos» (1984), produced the hit «La Esquina Caliente» shortly before the label folded."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"«Canción a un Individuo» and a bond with Colombia","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In the mid-1990s he wrote «Canción a un Individuo», inspired by the anonymous street dealers he observed near the Manhattan club El Corso, composing it in the vocal style of Héctor Lavoe in the hope that the ailing singer might record it. Bello also built a lasting bond with Colombia, especially Cali, where he recorded and toured extensively over the following decades and where, ultimately, his funeral would be held."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Legacy","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Days before 11 September 2001, Bello performed at one of the World Trade Center’s «Viernes de Salsa» concerts, dedicating «Basta Ya» to a world he described as threatened by nuclear weapons and corruption. He also played the preview party for a Rolling Stones film for a Hollywood crowd in the mid-1980s. Married to the bolero singer and designer Patricia González, he died after a fall in October 2025 injured his spine, having written on social media at the time: «No es un adiós, es un hasta luego, porque yo nací pa’ guarachar»."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', id, 1 FROM artists WHERE slug = 'jose-bello'
